<article id="post-1633" class="post-1633 post type-post status-publish format-standard hentry tag-emiliano-godoy tag-knitted-laced-stiched-sewn-or-woven">
	<header class="entry-header">
		<h1 class="entry-title">Knit Chair by Emiliano Godoy</h1>	</header><!-- .entry-header -->

	
	
	<div class="entry-content">
		<p><img data-recalc-dims="1" decoding="async" src="https://i0.wp.com/chairblog.eu/wp-content/uploads/2009/10/Knit-Chair-by-Emiliano-Godoy.jpg?resize=350%2C350&#038;ssl=1" alt="Knit Chair by Emiliano Godoy" title="Knit Chair by Emiliano Godoy" width="350" height="350" class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-5386" srcset="https://i0.wp.com/chairblog.eu/wp-content/uploads/2009/10/Knit-Chair-by-Emiliano-Godoy.jpg?w=350&amp;ssl=1 350w, https://i0.wp.com/chairblog.eu/wp-content/uploads/2009/10/Knit-Chair-by-Emiliano-Godoy.jpg?resize=150%2C150&amp;ssl=1 150w, https://i0.wp.com/chairblog.eu/wp-content/uploads/2009/10/Knit-Chair-by-Emiliano-Godoy.jpg?resize=300%2C300&amp;ssl=1 300w" sizes="(max-width: 350px) 85vw, 350px" /></p>
<p>Knit Chair by <a href="http://www.emilianogodoy.com" target="_blank">Emiliano Godoy</a></p>
<blockquote><p>design: Emiliano Godoy, 2004<br />
manufacture: Handmade by Pirwi in Mexico<br />
materials: FSC-certified beech or white oak, cotton rope<br />
dimensions: 61&#8243; long x 31&#8243; wide x 43&#8243; tall<br />
about: Consisting simply of wood panels and cotton rope (which holds everything together), this is one of the most inventive chairs we&#8217;ve ever seen.<br />
The Knit Chair won a Bronze Leaf at the 2005 International Furniture Design Fair in Asahikawa, Japan.<br />
Chair can be made in either FSC-certified beech or white oak. For samples of the woods in which this chair is available, please contact us.<br />
availability: This item is made to order, and ships within 3-4 weeks.<br />
price: $5,998.00 	</p></blockquote>
<p>Via  <br />Branch Home</p>
